extraction_notes: "WB2 printed 63-67 (cache p063-p067, page_offset 0): the Sunaj on printed 63-64 (the book tags the race NPC-only), the O.C.C. from printed 64 (A Secret Tattooed Man) through 66, its psionics and insanity on printed 67. Printed 65 is a full-page illustration. Printed 66 was rendered and matches the OCR. Imported as a PC although the book discourages it: Nate''s decision 2026-09-26 (survey, Decisions 2). || XP: the Sunaj Assassin ladder on printed 68, rendered and read off the image. || GROUP: no group heading in the book; the book calls it a warrior subclass, so men-of-arms. mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || RACE: always an Aerihman True Atlantean. Following undead-slayer and atlantean-monster-hunter, race_restrictions is only none and the True Atlantean racial block (printed 16) is in the True Atlanteans section. If a true-atlantean R.C.C. ships, revisit this line together with undead-slayer''s. The book gives the assassin all the True Atlantean abilities (printed 66), so the racial ability list, P.P.E. rule, saves (+2 vs magic of all kinds as spell_magic and ritual_magic, +4 vs horror factor) and Horror Factor 12 (the average Atlantean''s) are the racial block''s, not the Undead Slayer''s. || POOLS: M.D.C. 2D4x10 plus 11 (male) or 13 (female) per tattoo beyond six; the book counts nine starting tattoos and prints 2D4x10+33 for a male, so the female variant is 2d4x10+39. P.P.E. is not printed for the assassin: the racial rule, 10 base plus six per tattoo, gives 64 for nine tattoos (judgement: the Undead Slayer''s 2D4x10 +10/level P.P.E. is not extended to the Sunaj, whose page extends only the Slayer''s M.D.C. rule). No hit points or S.D.C. stored: a mega-damage being, as in the undead-slayer precedent. || TATTOOS: printed 66 lists The Marks of Heritage as the cross and the magic sword. Every other statement of the Marks (printed 16, 97) is a staked heart and a flaming sword, and printed 64 says the Sunaj hide the Marks of a True Atlantean, so the standard pair is granted and the cross is read as a slip; the count of nine (two Marks, Death Touch, one weapon, five powers) holds either way. The flaming sword is Tattoo: Weapon Covered in Flames. The starting power list omits the two powers already granted. Level grants at 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15 are one power tattoo each. || PSIONICS: major psionic as an attribute requirement and an O.C.C. feature (printed 66-67): eight powers from one category, or six from Physical, Sensitive and Healing combined, no Super. Modelled as a choice of four abilities, each carrying its own psionics block (the crocodillian precedent). I.S.P. M.E. plus 4D6, plus 1D6+1 per level. || SKILLS: Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+25; Tracking is Tracking (people) 25+20; Land Navigation 36+15 at 4 per level; Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+10; Disguise 25+20; Intelligence 32+15; Wilderness Survival 30+20; Prowl 25+10; Swimming 50+5. Languages and literacy as undead-slayer (Greek literacy is a Literacy: Other pick at 98). Three languages +10% as Language: Other picks. Hand to Hand: Assassin with no upgrade price printed, so no hand_to_hand block. || RELATED: six, plus two at each of levels four, eight and twelve. Mechanical and Science none; Electrical Basic Electronics only; Medical First Aid only (+5%). Secondary: four, limited the same way, no bonuses. || MONEY: 6D6x1000 credits stored; the 1D6x1000 in gold, gems or artifacts is not coin and is prose. || EQUIPMENT: named weapons mapped to the catalog''s common sets; Sunaj assassin environmental armor (printed 66: 110 M.D.C., 16 lbs, good mobility, -10% prowl, 85,000 to 100,000 credits) has no gear row, so the armor pick offers the alternatives the book names and the Sunaj armor is prose until the gear batch adds it. Pocket calculator, disguise make-up and a complete disguise, and the vehicle or riding animal have no rows and are prose."
---

## Lore

The Sunaj are the dark, masked warriors who travel the dimensions in the company of the Splugorth, never showing a face or an inch of bare skin. Rumor paints them as hideous, magic-steeped humanoids. The truth, which the Splugorth relish, is that the Sunaj are True Atlanteans of the Aerihman clan, who under the young Lord Aerihza have pledged themselves to conquest and to the secret extermination of every other Atlantean clan. Their monstrous helms hide handsome human faces and the Marks of Heritage. The name is Janus spelled backwards, for the two-faced Roman god of doorways.

The Sunaj assassin is the clan''s secret tattooed warrior, a subclass found only among the Aerihman: an assassin, spy and covert operative whose work is to find and kill the noble True Atlanteans, often by betraying the trust Atlanteans extend to any cousin. Assassins work in pairs and threes, sometimes sell their services as mercenaries to gain position and information for the new empire, and would rather die, and destroy their own bodies, than be captured and exposed. They care little for wealth; most give a large share of their fortunes to building the empire.

The book designs the Sunaj as villains for heroes to fight and warns players away from their secret. Imported here as an optional class, to be played with the GM''s consent.

Standard equipment typically includes a laser pulse rifle, a particle beam or plasma rifle, an energy pistol, a vibro sword or vibro claws, a vibro knife or neural mace, a laser scalpel, two silver-plated throwing knives and a cross of some kind. Sunaj love magic weapons and will acquire techno-wizard and other magic weapons whenever they can. A vehicle or riding animal suited to rough terrain (anything from a jet pack or hover cycle to a robot horse or gryphon). Other gear: disguise make-up and at least one complete disguise, backpack, 1D4 sacks, utility and ammo belts, sleeping bag, sunglasses and goggles, air filter, gas mask, 100 ft of rope, pocket tool kit, flashlight, canteen, compass, pocket calculator, and Sunaj assassin environmental armor or another medium to heavy M.D.C. armor such as CS Dead Boy, Gladiator, Crusader or Bushman. Money: 6D6x1000 credits plus 1D6x1000 in gold, gems or artifacts.

## Sunaj Assassin Environmental Armor

Light plate armor of Sunaj/Atlantean design, its helmet always shaped as a monster''s face. M.D.C. 110; weight 16 lbs (7.3 kg); good mobility, -10% to prowl. Black market cost 85,000 to 100,000 credits, sometimes sold in the Splugorth markets of Atlantis.

## Magic Tattoos

Nine to start: the two Marks of Heritage, Death Touch (a skull coiled with thorns), one magic weapon and five power tattoos of choice. One more power tattoo at every odd level from 3 to 15, at the clan elder''s or alchemist''s pleasure.

## True Atlanteans

The racial block the book prints for all True Atlanteans (printed 16), for a Sunaj assassin played with no R.C.C.:

- Alignment: the Sunaj are typically selfish or evil.
- Attributes: I.Q. 3D6+4, M.E. 4D6+6, M.A. 3D6+4, P.S. 4D6+4, P.P. 3D6, P.E. 3D6+6, P.B. 3D6+6, Spd 4D6+6.
- Hit Points: P.E. +1D6 per level. S.D.C.: 50 plus O.C.C., tattoo and physical skill S.D.C.; with seven or more tattoos the assassin is a mega-damage being instead.
- Horror Factor: 12 for the average Atlantean.
- P.P.E. base 10, plus 12 from the Marks of Heritage and six per additional tattoo.
- Height 6 ft plus 1D4 inches, plus an inch per century of age; weight 170 lbs and up. Appear 19 to 35 while anywhere from 19 to 250 years old; the average life span is 500 years.
- Appearance entirely human: tall, handsome, dark-haired.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sunaj-assassin');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sunaj-assassin';

